 "answer": "The environment variable is **`OLLAMA_MODELS`**. Set it to the directory where you want Ollama to store model files. By default on Windows, Ollama stores models in `%USERPROFILE%\\.ollama\\models`.\n\nOn Windows, you can set it persistently with PowerShell:\n\n```powershell\n[Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable(\"OLLAMA_MODELS\", \"D:\\OllamaModels\", \"User\")\n```\n\nThen restart Ollama (quit it from the system tray and relaunch) so the new value takes effect. You can also set it through the System Properties > Environment Variables dialog.",
